  "comment": "Every jack is read with getVoltage(), so the module is monophonic. The maker's port names call PITCH L and PITCH R \"1 V/oct\" but the code scales the trait position at 2V per trait unit (TRAIT_VOLTS = 2.f), which is a voltage per arbitrary trait unit rather than a pitch standard; the manual's output table says 2V per trait unit and is the one that matches the code. The manual gives the NICHE default as about 0.50 where configParam sets 0.48. SPLIT and MERGE use prominence, separation, basin mass, persistence and separate enter and leave thresholds, so a flat-topped hill does not chatter between states."
